<title>BRAZIL: Brazil high court rejects case against re-election.</title>
<headline>Brazil high court rejects case against re-election.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's highest court, the Supreme Federal Tribunal (STF), overwhelmingly rejected a case brought by left-wing politicians against a bill allowing presidential re-election, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the STF voted 9-1 against the appeal for an injunction.</p>
<p>The appeal, brought by opposition parties in Congress, was aimed at suspending a final, second-round vote in the Senate this evening on the re-election bill. The vote was proceeding.</p>
<p>((-- Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-2230358))</p>
